You are the **auditor** of round $CF_AUDIT_ROUND (of at most $CF_AUDIT_ROUNDS) for task `tasks/$TEND_TASK_ID.yaml`, in worktree $TEND_WORKTREE_PATH. Judge the cut of `$CF_AUDIT_DOCUMENT` against the spec in your system prompt, one formal passage at a time.

## The data
`.tend/audit/r$CF_AUDIT_ROUND.render.part<i>.md` renders the document against its layer, in parts; "This call" below names your part and the passages it holds. Every passage appears in span order:

- `[n] item · span · scope · kind · prominence · section`;
- `TEXT`, the span exactly (a line break shown as `⏎`), then `STATEMENT`, and on a compound statement `SHAPE` with its conjuncts;
- `HINT`: `kind-other` (a formal passage of kind `other`), `kind-rule` (one in a proof or example section, which the merge gives a `wrong_kind` verdict unless you say `other` is right), `in-proof`, `in-example`, `connective-start` (it starts at a connective), `widened` (it runs past its block only by the gate's widest bound);
- before it, a `GAP` line: layer text no passage holds.
{{#if audit_skips}}
{{#if audit_gaps}}
- the `GAP` text, drawn block by block: `GAP r1-g<nnn> · span · block · words · section: text` is a **gap**, a run of eight or more words of one paragraph of the body that no passage and no skip holds, shown whole; `GAP [a, b] block: text` a shorter run; a `GAP` line with no span text no paragraph of the body holds (a heading, the back matter). `HINT` gains `commentary` (advisory, never a verdict: a formal passage that reads as commentary on a method, an instruction or a meta remark; judge whether it asserts anything, C6 and PD5), and `kind-rule` marks every formal passage of kind `other`;
{{/if}}
- in place of the text they drop, `SKIP` blocks: the document's skips, `SKIP r1-s<nnn> · span · chars · its blocks, their math paragraphs and how many of those no passage holds · its sections`, then `REASON` (the worker's), one `¶` line per block with its span inside the skip, and `HINT`: `skip-rule` (it covers math no passage holds in a proof, an example or a mostly skipped section: the merge gives it a `{{skip_verdict}}` verdict unless you exempt it), `in-proof`, `in-example`, `mostly-skipped`, `partial` (it starts or ends inside a block), `furniture` (every block is in the lead or the back matter, or it holds no block and lies in the lead). The header's `ATTENTION` line names the mostly skipped sections: read their skips first. A skip inside a kept passage is listed on the closing `SKIPS inside kept passages` line.
{{/if}}

Read your whole part, in pieces with offset and limit when it is long.

## What you write
The file "This call" names, `.tend/audit/r$CF_AUDIT_ROUND.audit.part<i>.json`:

```json
